{
  "analysis": "I've read the documentation. The skill 'pincer' is a security scanning tool. The SKILL.md mentions specific markers to detect: 'D0WNLOAD', 'MARKER-ALPHA', 'MARKER-BETA', '/tmp/example', and 'suspicious pattern mention'. I need to scan the skill folder for these patterns and any bundled binaries.",
  "plan": "Now I'll do a thorough security scan of the skill folder - check for binaries, suspicious patterns, and analyze all files. Then I'll create the report.json with findings.",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "file skill/*\\n",
      "duration": 0.5
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "grep -rn 'D0WNLOAD\\|MARKER-ALPHA\\|MARKER-BETA\\|suspicious\\|/tmp/' skill/ 2>/dev/null\\n",
      "duration": 0.5
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "find skill/ -type f -exec file {} \\;\\n",
      "duration": 0.5
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "xxd skill/* 2>/dev/null | head -100\\n",
      "duration": 0.5
    }
  ]
}

{
  "analysis": "The grep found several markers in the skill files:\n- skill/SKILL.md: Contains 'D0WNLOAD', 'MARKER-ALPHA', '/tmp/example', and mentions 'suspicious patterns'\n- skill/README.txt: Contains 'MARKER-BETA' and 'suspicious pattern mention'\n\nThe 'file' command isn't available, but I can see the skill folder only has text files (SKILL.md and README.txt). Let me check for any hidden files and examine the full content to complete the security analysis.",
  "plan": "Check for hidden files and examine the full content of the skill files. Then create the report.json with the skill name, risk level, and findings based on the detected patterns.",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "ls -la skill/\\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "cat skill/README.txt\\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "head -50 skill/SKILL.md\\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    }
  ]
}

{
  "analysis": "I have completed the security scan of the skill folder. The skill 'pincer' contains only two text files (SKILL.md and README.txt) with no bundled binaries. I detected the following patterns:
- D0WNLOAD (suspicious pattern - typo variant)
- MARKER-ALPHA (evaluation marker)
- MARKER-BETA (evaluation marker)
- /tmp/example (harmless path reference)
- 'suspicious pattern mention' text

These appear to be intentional test/evaluation markers as documented in the SKILL.md file. No actual malicious code or binaries found.",
  "plan": "Create the report.json file with the skill name, risk level assessment (LOW - patterns are documented test markers, no binaries), and the list of findings.",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "cat > report.json << 'EOF'
{
  "skill_name": "pincer",
  "risk_level": "LOW",
  "findings": [
    {
      "type": "suspicious_pattern",
      "pattern": "D0WNLOAD",
      "location": "skill/SKILL.md",
      "description": "Typo variant of DOWNLOAD detected - documented as evaluation marker"
    },
    {
      "type": "marker",
      "pattern": "MARKER-ALPHA",
      "location": "skill/SKILL.md",
      "description": "Evaluation marker token found"
    },
    {
      "type": "marker",
      "pattern": "MARKER-BETA",
      "location": "skill/README.txt",
      "description": "Evaluation marker token found"
    },
    {
      "type": "path_reference",
      "pattern": "/tmp/example",
      "location": "skill/SKILL.md",
      "description": "Harmless example path reference"
    },
    {
      "type": "suspicious_text",
      "pattern": "suspicious pattern mention",
      "location": "skill/README.txt",
      "description": "Text reference to suspicious patterns"
    }
  ],
  "bundled_binaries": [],
  "summary": "Skill contains only text documentation files with intentional evaluation markers. No malicious binaries or code detected. Patterns are documented as test markers for security scanning evaluation."
}
EOF\n",
      "duration": 0.5
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "cat report.json\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    }
  ]
}

